post("PL-12", "planning", "reel",
     "“Removal of the conservatory to form a single storey extension”",
     "THE CONSERVATORY IS NOT A CONSERVATORY.\n\nIt was an extension with no foundations, no insulation and no planning permission, built in 1993 out of uPVC and optimism.\n\nAnd the application to replace it reads: “REMOVAL OF THE CONSERVATORY TO FORM A SINGLE STOREY EXTENSION.”\n\nUnderneath that sentence is the easiest nine-window job in the county, because the shell is already there and the ground floor is already high.\n\nRead the description. That is where the money is.",
     "Photorealistic 9:16 shot of a UK rear elevation with a white uPVC conservatory attached to a brick house, sunlight glinting off it, a view through to a dark scruffy extension beyond, sky and rain clouds, slightly melancholy and cinematic",
     "photo-real", "planning", img="9:16", cta="Planning search, filtered to window work. fenora.pro/job-finder")

post("PL-13", "planning", "static",
     "The non-material amendment. Free money, nobody uses it.",
     "NON-MATERIAL AMENDMENT APPROVED.\n\nThat is the whole email. Six words. It means someone changed the spec slightly after approval and the council said yes.\n\nA non-material amendment is a free, fast, low-stakes permission to change your window specification after the application was approved. A different colour. A different bar profile. A different glass.\n\nEvery one of those is a £40 item on a £900 window and it is the difference between winning the job and not. It takes one phone call. Almost nobody makes the call.",
     "Photorealistic close-up of an email on a phone screen showing a short official approval message, sitting on top of a workbench beside a RAL swatch and a window frame sample, morning light, quietly triumphant",
     "photo-real", "planning", cta="Track what a job is worth before you knock on the door. fenora.pro")

